I've always found that to be a major weakness of boulder traps. They 
shouldn't be that obvious! I propose that all boulder-trap boulders be 
hidden in closets until the trap is triggered, at which point they come 
crashing out through the secret door, flattening everything in their 
path and then settle neatly into another closet in the opposite wall, 
ready for reuse.
Disabling them would then necessitate a bit of digging work or possibly 
blocking the boulder's path with other boulders, which I feel would be a 
lot more rewarding and would really enhance the entire trap-disabling 
experience for the player.
Oh, and putting a fresh boulder in the opposite, empty boulder-closet 
obviously creates a much more /lethal/ trap, though you'd probably have 
to manually reset that one every time. These aren't exactly billard 
balls we're dealing with here.

